    historical_tag: Some("The Red River War of 1874-1875 was the last major campaign by the U.S. Army against the Southern Plains tribes. Following the attack on Adobe Walls in June 1874, the Army launched a winter campaign under Generals Philip Sheridan, Nelson A. Miles, and Ranald S. Mackenzie, systematically hunting down Comanche, Kiowa, and Cheyenne bands across the Texas Panhandle. The campaign marked the end of organized Native resistance on the Southern Plains."),
